diff --git a/packages/interaction/user-approval/README.md b/packages/interaction/user-approval/README.md
index 8c52fa090..6c92de1dc 100644
--- a/packages/interaction/user-approval/README.md
+++ b/packages/interaction/user-approval/README.md
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@ These limits define when the seam is a poor fit or needs special composition car
 
 - **Requests are valid only inside an open turn** — an idle or between-turn caller throws before auditing; a durable out-of-turn approval workflow is deferred.
 - **Only one-shot grants exist** — the outcome vocabulary has `allowed-once` but no `allow-always`, remembered rule, revocation, or grant store; session policy is only `ask` / `never`.
-- **The request carries no tool arguments** — an answerer sees the tool name, reason, and optional call id; the ACP machine channel requires a call id and delegates requests without one.
+- **Tool arguments are opt-in and asker-supplied** — `arguments` is optional on the request; an answerer sees it only when the asker attached it (`dsh-tools`' `serviceAsk` does, passing the call's parsed input), and an asker that omits it (or one written before this field existed) still gets a request with `arguments: undefined`. The seam does not validate the shape itself. The ACP machine channel requires a call id and delegates requests without one.
 - **No built-in answerer** — headless or incompletely composed deployments resolve `unavailable` and fail closed; the service itself never prompts a human.
 
